# Breaking-Change Major Version Protocol

RULE: When a library or service makes a breaking change, the commit message MUST trigger a major version bump. All downstream consumer repos MUST update their `pyproject.toml` dependency constraint to the new major range before their next merge to main.

WHY: The CI version-bump reads the commit prefix to determine semver. A breaking change without the correct prefix stays at the old major version, causing consumers to silently receive a broken API.

CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md, 04-architecture/TIER-ARCHITECTURE.md

---

## What Counts as a Breaking Change

A change is BREAKING (requires major bump) when **any consumer repo must change their code, config, scripts, or schema handling** to adopt it.

### API and Type System

| Example                                                            | Breaking?     |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------- |
| Remove a public class, function, or method                         | ✅ YES        |
| Rename a public class, function, or method                         | ✅ YES        |
| Add a **required** parameter to a function                         | ✅ YES        |
| Remove a parameter from a function                                 | ✅ YES        |
| Remove a default value (parameter becomes required)                | ✅ YES        |
| Move a symbol to a different module path                           | ✅ YES        |
| Remove a re-export from `__init__.py`                              | ✅ YES        |
| Change a return type incompatibly (narrow, widen, or replace)      | ✅ YES        |
| Rename or remove an exception/error class consumers catch          | ✅ YES        |
| Change exception hierarchy (consumers catching parent class break) | ✅ YES        |
| Add a required abstract method to a base class or Protocol         | ✅ YES        |
| Remove or rename an Enum value                                     | ✅ YES        |
| Add an **optional** parameter with a default                       | ❌ NO (minor) |
| Add a new public function or class                                 | ❌ NO (minor) |
| Fix a bug without changing the public interface                    | ❌ NO (patch) |

### Data Schemas and Storage (cloud-agnostic)

| Example                                                                        | Breaking?     |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------- |
| Rename or remove a Parquet/storage schema column                               | ✅ YES        |
| Change a column type (e.g. `string` → `int`)                                   | ✅ YES        |
| Change a Pydantic model field name, type, or remove it                         | ✅ YES        |
| Add a **required** field to a Pydantic model (no default)                      | ✅ YES        |
| Change event/message schema on any message bus (Pub/Sub, Kafka, Redis Streams) | ✅ YES        |
| Change GCS/S3/object-store path structure consumers read from                  | ✅ YES        |
| Add an **optional** field to a Pydantic model (with default)                   | ❌ NO (minor) |
| Add a new column to a schema with a nullable/default value                     | ❌ NO (minor) |

### Configuration and Environment

| Example                                                                          | Breaking?     |
| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- |
| Rename a config key or environment variable consumers must set                   | ✅ YES        |
| Remove a config key consumers rely on                                            | ✅ YES        |
| Change the expected type or format of a config value                             | ✅ YES        |
| Change a CLI argument name or remove it                                          | ✅ YES        |
| Raise the minimum required version of a dependency (forces consumers to upgrade) | ✅ YES        |
| Add a new optional config key with a sensible default                            | ❌ NO (minor) |

### Runtime Behavior

| Example                                                   | Breaking?     |
| --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- |
| Change a storage path format consumers construct or parse | ✅ YES        |
| Change topic/queue/channel names on a message bus         | ✅ YES        |
| Remove a REST or gRPC endpoint                            | ✅ YES        |
| Change an endpoint's request/response schema              | ✅ YES        |
| Change authentication method or token format              | ✅ YES        |
| Add a new endpoint                                        | ❌ NO (minor) |
| Add optional fields to a request schema                   | ❌ NO (minor) |

