## Pre-1.0.0 Safety Rule

If a repo is still at `0.x.x`, the CI treats **major bumps as minor** (never auto-jumps to `1.0.0`). This is intentional — `0.x.x` signals an unstable API where breaking changes are expected.

To graduate a repo to `1.0.0`, directly edit `pyproject.toml` to `version = "1.0.0"` and commit with `chore:`. This is a one-time manual act — the CI will not do it automatically. From `1.0.0` onwards, normal semver bump rules apply.

